tal Bytes: 27292\\nShowing lines 490 to 537\\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: \n<truncated 29732 bytes>\nat least 3, thus validating the inequality.\\n\\n**Extending the Radius Analysis**\\n\\nConsidering the case of graphs with a radius of 4. Investigated whether the total domination number can be less than 4 in such graphs.\\n\\n\\n**Bounding Total Domination for Radius 4**\\n\\nDetermined the total domination number, $\\\\gamma_t(G)$, cannot be 1, 2, or 3 if the graph radius, $\\\\text{rad}(G)$, is 4.  Showed that if $\\\\gamma_t(G)$ were 3, this would lead to a contradiction, where radius would be at most 2.\\n\\n**Testing Counterexample for Radius 5**\\n\\nNow considering if graph radius equals 5, whether the total domination number can be less than or equal to 4. Examined if this condition is possible. Considered the previous case with $\\\\gamma_t(G)=4$ to check the conditions.\\n\\n\\n**Bounding Eccentricity in Connected Graphs**\\n\\nDetermined that a vertex $b$ has eccentricity at most 3 in the cases examined. Observed that the graph radius, $\\\\text{rad}(G)$, is at most 3 in all connected cases. Investigated the disconnected case where $G[S]$ consists of two disjoint edges,  $e_1$ and $e_2$.\\n\\n**Analyzing Path Length Between Disjoint Edges**\\n\\nEstablished that the distance between edges $e_1$ and $e_2$, denoted $d(e_1, e_2)$, represents the shortest path between them. Concluded that every vertex on such a path has a neighbor in $S$. Examined if the path length $L$ can be greater than or equal to 4.\\n\\n**Bounding Path Length in Disconnected S**\\n\\nReasoned that a path length $L \\\\ge 4$ implies a vertex $v_2$ is at a distance of at least 2 from both $e_1$ and $e_2$. Deduced that if $v_2$ has a neighbor in $e_1$ or $e_2$, the path length can be shortened. Concluded the path length $L$ must be at most 3, due to contradiction.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"search_web\",\"args\":{\"query\":\"\\\"radius total domination number\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching the web\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search radius total domination number\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n22: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
