x tuples: the cograph test is four nested\\n99: # quantifiers, so an 8-vertex witness needs 8⁴ steps. Measured at n = 8 — the\\n100: # default depth fails on cograph (connected/tree/claw-free still pass), this\\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n10: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":221,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:47:28Z","thinking":"**Shifting to refutation graph search**\n\nThe objective has changed: instead of proving the radius-domination inequality, focus shifts to finding a graph that *disproves* it. This requires constructing a refutation strategy, specifically looking for graphs where the radius is strictly greater than the total domination number. Previous efforts to prove the inequality are no longer the primary concern.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating the objective's scope**\n\nThe focus is now on the prompt's wording, specifically \"neither was\" as a potential valid result if a proof or refutation cannot be found. This suggests a shift to determining whether the conjecture is provable within constraints or if a definitive answer is unattainable. Understanding the structure of the `Candidate` proposition in Lean 4 is essential to assess its provability and to recognize a valid termination condition.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Scratch file to test lean definitions\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\n#check GraphCalc.radius\\n#check GraphCalc.totalDominationNumber\\n\"","Description":"\"Create scratch.lean to test definitions\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc/scratch.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Writing scratch.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"Write scratch.lean\""}}]}
